  - src/App.css
decisions:
  - id: mobile-os-notifications
    decision: Fire mobile alarms via OS-scheduled local notifications instead of the JS timer
    rationale: Mobile OSes freeze background JS timers, so the in-app scheduler can't fire when the app is closed/locked. Handing each enabled alarm to the OS (one-shot or weekly interval) is the only way it reliably fires; the rich in-app overlay still runs when foreground.
  - id: youtube-embed-fallback
    decision: Harden the YouTube embed AND add an 'Open on YouTube' browser fallback
    rationale: YouTube Error 153 is an origin/referrer rejection; a webview's custom-scheme origin is opaque so the embed is inherently unreliable off localhost. The origin/nocookie/referrer changes fix dev; the browser-open fallback guarantees the video always plays regardless of context.
learnings:
  - YouTube embed Error 153 stems from origin/referrer trust; sending a real http(s) origin + youtube-nocookie.com + a referrerPolicy helps on localhost, but a Tauri custom-scheme origin stays opaque so embeds remain flaky in the installed/mobile app — an openUrl-to-browser fallback is the dependable path.
  - Tauri notification plugin ScheduleInterval weekday is 1=Sunday..7=Saturday (our model is 0=Sun..6=Sat, so add 1); notification ids must be 32-bit ints.
  - Local audio/video files are the most reliable in-app alarm trigger across platforms; YouTube is best-effort.
